  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Innovative Financing Facility for Climate in Asia and the Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Innovative Financing Facility for Climate in Asia and the Pacific (IFCAP) is a multi-donor financing mechanism established by the Asian Development Bank (ADB). Through IFCAP, development partners contribute a combination of grants and guarantees to the ADB, which will unlock new climate-focused lending from the Bank. The $280m UK guarantee to support IFCAP will unlock up to $1.2bn of additional, affordable climate finance from the ADB for middle-income countries in Asia and the Pacific.</narrative>
  </description>
